{"chunk_id": "c32cdc51bff0", "text": "Rama and Lakshmana discover the dying vulture king Jatayu, who had tried to rescue Sita from Ravana during the abduction. Gravely wounded with his wings severed, Jatayu recounts how Ravana seized Sita and fled south. Even in his final moments he offers prophetic reassurance: the time of the abduction is auspicious for recovery, and Ravana will soon perish like a fish swallowing a hook. After revealing Ravana\u2019s lineage, Jatayu dies. Rama is overcome with grief, declaring he mourns the noble bird even more than Sita\u2019s abduction because Jatayu sacrificed his life in loyal defense. Honoring him like a father, Rama performs full funeral rites and cremates him. The episode highlights dharma, devotion beyond species, and foreshadows Ravana\u2019s downfall.\nMortally wounded Jatayu tells Rama Ravana carried Sita south, then dies; Rama mourns deeply and performs funeral rites for the heroic vulture.\nThemes: sacrifice and loyalty, grief and compassion, dharma and duty, omens of Ravana's downfall", "vector": [-0.0069312285631895065, -0.02238083817064762, -0.002990138716995716, 0.005411046091467142, -0.02398807927966118, 0.014987526461482048, -0.038332708179950714, -0.014826802536845207, -0.013795489445328712, -0.022581743076443672, 0.01540273055434227, 0.01583132892847061, 0.011505169793963432, 0.015429518185555935, -0.007915664464235306, -0.008062995038926601, 0.036162931472063065, -0.0077080619521439075, 0.04004709795117378, -0.024952422827482224, 0.005357471760362387, -0.0055181956849992275, -0.014920557849109173, 0.016554586589336395, -0.0015093002002686262, 0.007105346769094467, 0.014491960406303406, -0.03343062102794647, 0.032412704080343246, -0.0077147590927779675, -0.007949148304760456, -0.003448872361332178, -0.021376311779022217, -0.015978658571839333, -0.01329992339015007, 0.010426978580653667, 0.008143357001245022, -0.012918203137814999, 0.02022445574402809, 0.001796427182853222, 0.004851859994232655, -0.002266880124